[12664]="70029A58\n1\tAccompany Tomos to establish a fair alliance between the people of Galtrev and the White Hand\tTomos is at the outskirts of the Dragon-clan's encampment in western Pren Gwydh. You should speak with Tomos to travel to Galtrev.\n2\tTalk to Mari\tMari is in Galtrev, the main village of Pren Gwydh. You should speak with Mari in Galtrev.\n",
[12665]="700586F9\n1\tTalk to Derwent Bindweed outside the town of Stoneheight\tDerwent Bindweed is outside the town of Stoneheight, north-east of Amon Raith in the North Downs.\n2\tTalk to Derwent Bindweed and tour the town of Stoneheight\tDerwent Bindweed is outside the town of Stoneheight, at Annúndir in the North Downs.\n3\tTalk to Derwent Bindweed in Stoneheight\tDerwent Bindweed is in the town of Stoneheight in the North Downs.\n4\tTalk to Brom Hawksbeard in the Bree Jail\tBrom Hawksbeard is in the Bree Jail.\n",
[12666]="70028261\n1\tFree men of Lhan Tarren from their cages (total: 6)\tThe White Hand encampment is in the south-eastern part of Trum Dreng, and this is where the half-orc soldiers retreated with the kidnapped men of Lhan Tarren. You should search the encampment for the men and free them as you find them.\n2\tTalk to Chief Guto\tChief Guto can be found in Lhan Tarren, where Elder Riagán once stood. You should seek out Chief Guto and tell him that you have freed the captured Stag-clan.\n",
[12667]="700032D8\n1\tTalk to Callum\tCallum's camp-site is on the far west side of the Frogmoors, west of Budgeford. In light of the revelations gleaned from Callum's journal, Wilimar Bolger has asked you to go to Callum's camp and stop him from carrying out his intended revenge.\n2\tTalk to Wilimar Bolger\tWilimar Bolger can be found near his hole on the north-west side of Budgeford. When you arrived at Callum's camp-site, you found him wounded. Racked with pain, he told of how he had fled from his hiding place near Wilimar's home, only to startle a wild boar, which gored him. He feels that he will soon succumb to his wounds and told you to let Wilimar know he has nothing more to fear.\n",
[12668]="7002F898\n1\tTalk to Guthléod about Dagarm's whereabouts\tGuthléod can be found within the trader's outpost west of Elthengels. Ofrith has suggested asking Guthléod about Dagarm's last known whereabouts.\n2\tSearch for the missing trader, Dagarm\tDagarm was last known to be heading south and east, beyond the river. Guthléod believes that Dagarm may have headed beyond the river and towards known enemy territory. He has cautioned you to be careful as you search.\n3\tFree Dagarm from capture\tDagarm appears to have been captured by the Uruks in the camp beyond the river. Dagarm wishes to be released from his captivity within the Uruk-hai camp. You may be able to undo the ropes that bind him.\n4\tTalk to Dagarm at the trader's outpost\tDagarm has returned to the trader's outpost along the road west of Elthengels. You have freed Dagarm, and he has asked you to speak with him upon your return to the trader's outpost.\n",
[12669]="7000BFCC\n1\tDefeat Narnûlubat\030Defeat Zogtark\tNarnûlubat and Zogtark can be found within Noruidor. Tortrygg has asked to you to find and defeat two of the leaders of the Ghâshfra, Narnûlubat and Zogtark.\n2\tTalk to Tortrygg\tTortrygg is at the Eldgang camp within the Rift of Nûrz Ghâshu. You should return to Tortrygg with news of your victory against Narnûlubat and Zogtark.\n",
[12670]="7004527C\n1\tDefeat Warg-rider message-bearers (total: 10)\tYou should defeat any Warg-rider message-bearers you find in the Beacon Hills.\n2\tReturn to Déorwine\tReturn to Déorwine in the camp in Taur Drúadan and tell him of the Warg-rider message-bearers you defeated.\n",
[12671]="7001BA18\n1\tEnter the fight-arena before the fight begins. Do not leave the bounds\tThe fight-arena is the lowered floorspace in the centre of the hall, marked by green banners. The dwarf-club is in your inventory. Gísli Strongclub has given you an excellent weapon with which to defend your prize. You should enter the fight-arena below while wielding your mighty dwarf-club. WARNING: If you leave the fight-arena after entering, you will drop your club. The club may not be used outside of the fight-arena's bounds. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tSlot the dwarf-club in your skills and wait for the fight to begin\tThe fight-arena's bounds are in the centre of the ale-hall at Thorin's Hall, marked by green banners. You should wait for the fight to begin. WARNING: If you leave the arena's bounds after entering, you will drop your mighty dwarf-club. The dwarf-club cannot be used outside of the arena's bounds. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tCollect the glorious beer before the others get the last of it\030Give greedy fellow players a whack for good measure (total: 3)\tGreedy people in the lowered fight-arena wish to steal the glorious beer. Give the greedy folks around you a few good whacks for their impertinence! You must now do whatever it takes to collect the glorious beer for yourself, but beware: if you leave the fight-arena for any reason, you will be disqualified. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tTalk to Gísli Strongclub before the time expires\tGísli Strongclub is in the arena at Thorin's Hall. You should speak with Gísli Strongclub to boast of your excellence in collecting the glorious beer. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[12672]="7002AC95\n1\tEnter the fight-arena before the fight begins. Do not leave the bounds\tThe fight-arena is the lowered floorspace in the centre of the arena, marked by green banners. The dwarf-club is in your inventory. Gísli Strongclub has given you an excellent weapon to use during the contest. You should enter the fight-arena below while wielding your mighty dwarf-club. WARNING: If you leave the fight-arena after entering, your club will not be usable outside of the fight-arena's bounds. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tSlot the dwarf-club in your skills and wait for the fight to begin\tThe fight-arena's bounds are in the centre of the ale-hall at Thorin's Hall, marked by green banners. You should wait for the fight to begin. WARNING: If you leave the fight-arena and the contest begins, you will fail the quest.\n3\tGive fellow players a whack for good measure (total: 8)\tShow everyone that you are a mighty competitor, give the other participants a good whack and send them reeling! Some competitors may stop moving to take the glorious beer, knock them away while you can! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tTalk to Gísli Strongclub before the time expires\tGísli Strongclub is in the arena at Thorin's Hall. You should speak with Gísli Strongclub to boast of your excellence in the glorious beer event. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
})
